<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2018/08/Tim-Cook-Steve-Jobs.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="alignleft size-full wp-image-1060212" />15 years ago today, Tim Cook was appointed Apple CEO following Steve Jobs' resignation on August 24, 2011. On September 1, Cook will step down and incoming CEO John Ternus will <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/20/tim-cook-stepping-down/">take over</a>, ahead of Apple announcing new iPhone 18 Pro models and its first foldable iPhone. <br/>
<br/>
